# No longer provisional. Grounded in "Intro Focus 23" (Wave VII - Voyager,
# CD1-2): the tape passes through Focus 22 on the way from 21 to 23 and
# describes it in some detail, but says "22" and "twenty-two" without always
# pairing the word "focus" right next to the number, so the library's
# automated Library.sourceCoverage() scan (which looks for the literal
# "focus <digits>" pattern) still reports 0 for this level -- a known
# scanner limitation, not evidence the corpus is actually silent here. This
# briefing exists precisely because it is not.

@segment     briefing-f22
@title       Focus 22 — Here and There
@levels      F22
@duration    ~1m

say You are now in Focus 22.
pause 5
say This area is heavily populated, though only a small part of those here are conscious the way you are right now.
pause 8
say Some have altered their awareness through substances, or through injury — not fully conscious, their perception of the physical distorted.
pause 8
say Others are millions of people in ordinary physical sleep. Only part of their awareness has come here. Most aren't in control of what they're experiencing — they're running on patterns pulled straight from physical life, so completely that nothing else exists to them right now. Dreams. Dreaming.
pause 10
say You won't interrupt them if you move among them. You likely won't even perceive what they're dreaming — it belongs to each of them alone.
pause 8
say You're in full control here, whether or not they are. Observe, if you like. You're always free to move on toward Focus 23.
pause 8
